    {
      "definition": "**Dissociatives** are a subclass of hallucinogen that produce a feeling of detachment from the body, the sense of self, and the surroundings. Dissociatives mainly block NMDA receptors, which are part of the glutamate system. This system binds sensory information and the sense of self into one coherent experience. The block interrupts this system and creates the sense of disconnection. At low doses, the effect is a floaty, dreamlike state. At high doses, the effect is a full out-of-body experience.",
      "warning": "",
