    {
      "definition": "**Entactogens** (also known as empathogens) are a class of psychoactive substances that produce emotional openness, empathy, warmth, and closeness to other people. Entactogens mainly cause a large release of serotonin, with some dopamine and noradrenaline. This mix makes the experience mildly euphoric and social, not strongly hallucinatory. The name comes from the Greek *en* (\"within\"), the Latin *tactus* (\"touch\"), and *-gen* (\"to produce\"). Together these parts mean \"to touch within.\"",
      "warning": "",
