    {
      "definition": "**Antipsychotics** (also known as neuroleptics) are a class of psychoactive medications that manage psychosis. Psychosis includes hallucinations, delusions, and disordered thought. Antipsychotics mainly block dopamine receptors. This block reduces dopamine signaling, which is too high during a psychotic state.",
      "warning": "",
      "columns": {
        "1": 0,
