    {
      "definition": "**Opioids** are a class of psychoactive substances that relieve pain and produce euphoria, relaxation, and contentment. They also cause sedation. At high doses, opioids slow breathing to a dangerous degree. Opioids imitate endorphins, the natural painkilling chemicals of the body, and act on the same opioid receptors. The name comes from *opium*, the extract of the poppy, and *-oid* (\"resembling\"). The term \"opiate\" covers only natural poppy derivatives, but \"opioid\" covers any substance that acts on these receptors.",
      "warning": "",
