    {
      "definition": "**Cannabinoids** are a class of psychoactive substances that change mood, appetite, memory, perception, and pain through the endocannabinoid system of the body. They act on the CB1 receptors that the body's own cannabis-like signal chemicals normally use. Common effects are relaxation, a changed sense of time, and more appetite. The name comes from the *Cannabis* plant, where these compounds were first identified.",
      "warning": "",
